en select the question mark $(\\text{?}).$\n\n|  | $2$ | $4$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $2$ | $1$ | {{field-1}} | $0$ |\n| $4$ | $1$ | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |\n| $6$ | {{field-4}} | $1$ | $0$ |" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the following definitions:\n\n- A binary relation $R,$ defined on a set $A,$ is *symmetric* if for all $x,y\\in A,$ we have\n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\,⟹\\,(y,x)\\in R.\n$$\n\nIn other words, if a pair $(x,y)$ belongs to a symmetric relation, then the pair $(y,x)$ should also be in the relation.\n\n- A binary relation $R,$ defined on a set $A,$ is *antisymmetric* if for all $x,y\\in A,$ we have\n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\,\\text{and}\\,(y,x)\\in R\\,⟹\\,x=y.\n$$\n\nIn other words, only one of the pairs, either $(x,y)$ or $(y,x),$ can be in an antisymmetric relation. Note that this condition allows pairs of the form $(x,x).$\n\nWe are given elements of the adjacency matrix in the following highlighted cells outside the diagonal:  \n\n|  | $2$ | $4$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $2$ | $1$ |  | $0$ |\n| $4$ | $1$ |  |  |\n| $6$ |  | $1$ | $0$ |\n\nAs a result, the relation contains the pairs $(4,2)$ and $(6,4).$ Since $R$ must be symmetric, we require \n\n$$\n(2,4)\\in R,\\,(4,6)\\in R.\n$$\n\nSo, the cells corresponding to these elements must all equal $1.$\n\n|  | $2$ | $4$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $2$ | $1$ | $1$ | $0$ |\n| $4$ | $1$ |  | $1$ |\n| $6$ |  | $1$ | $0$ |\n\nAlso, note the following:\n\n- The symmetric relation condition is equivalent to $(x,y)\\notin R⟹(y,x)\\notin R.$ Therefore, $(2,6)\\notin R$ implies $(6,2)\\notin R.$\n\n- We do not have enough information to determine whether $(4,4)$ is an element of $R.$\n\nLet's add this information to our table.\n\n|  | $2$ | $4$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $2$ | $1$ | $1$ | $0$ |\n| $4$ | $1$ | $?$ | $1$ |\n| $6$ | $0$ | $1$ | $0$ |"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186417611 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203925 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f60a9114-56fc-5360-ae43-4601b4dee096" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Symmetric and Antisymmetric Relations From Adjacency Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2bf4e591-e60b-5f2c-a32d-a8b7ba26375c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{?}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417406} {:answer/id #uuid "96c2284d-40ee-5b0b-b5bf-e353e6d52e3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417475} {:answer/id #uuid "c03158e7-b90f-5604-a985-ced43e1f6a0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417500}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2bf4e591-e60b-5f2c-a32d-a8b7ba26375c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{?}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417406} :answer-field/id #uuid "41f24ffc-7eba-575c-90b8-e448a2dc7f23" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417562} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "916eec5c-e0d8-5b2c-8bc9-3a5f5acf6a56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417472} {:answer/id #uuid "9a1a5e33-077c-5105-bb24-ef1f9aa49813" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417476} {:answer/id #uuid "fdc498a9-fdee-5b9b-b096-cea07571b6a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{?}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417547}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9a1a5e33-077c-5105-bb24-ef1f9aa49813" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417476} :answer-field/id #uuid "6915c63d-35f9-5f95-8e62-98c1